<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Raynald of Châtillon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1125–1187</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Reynald of Châtillon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Raynald of Châtillon was a French knight who became Prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> by marriage in 1153 and, after years as a captive in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a>, Lord of Oultrejordain through his marriage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephanie-of-milly">Stephanie of Milly</a> in 1176. From <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-karak">Kerak</a> he raided Muslim caravans and in 1182–1183 sent ships into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sea">Red Sea</a>, provoking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a>. Captured at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hattin">Battle of Hattin</a> in 1187, he was executed by Saladin himself.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/raynald-of-chatillon.jpg" alt="Raynald of Châtillon" width="320" height="311" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ReynaldofChatillon%26PatriarchofAntioch.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
